## Native receipts and cleanup

Artifact `10311973890` is a 3,568-byte ZIP with four exact members and SHA-256
`eef36461a2f0e7b549963c9cc2c148f9336864327bdf46c71f1ab5d3f1ac78ac`.
Only its four validated JSON receipts were saved locally, 9,121 bytes total,
inside a mode-700 directory with mode-600 files. No ZIP, token, signed URL or
raw job log was retained.

- `wrong_entry`: expected `entry_binding_rejected`, worker exit 1; case passed.
- `wrong_manifest`: expected `source_binding_rejected`, worker exit 1; case passed.
- `positive`: one successful tiny import, worker exit 0; case passed.

The positive generated fixture has 736 model parameters, nine input files and
28,736 generated input bytes. It reports two checkpoint audits and two tokenizer
audits, zero forward calls and zero optimizer steps. These are synthetic inputs,
not the user's pretrained checkpoint or dataset.

Each case confirms its owned cgroup emptied/removed and workload reaped. The
outer supervisor needed zero TERM/KILL attempts and reaped zero unexpected
adopted children. The separate case guardians each recorded one cleanup kill
attempt; those must not be confused with outer-supervisor signal counts.
Owned container/image absence and the acquired input's exact retirement passed.

## Audit bounds and retained limitations

Post-run acquisition/status used 13 of 16 GETs, including the one authenticated
artifact redirect and one credential-free ZIP GET. A first metadata decoder
rejected an unmodelled step state; a later fresh observation supported pending
states. One local download-helper literal error occurred before any request.
Neither event retried or changed the remote workflow; both remain in the report.

The native/source/software pins and old evidence are intact. In the local agent
and new qualification, no local native harness execution, actual model/tokenizer/
dataset payload read, AWS action, GPU, inference, training or extra push occurred.
Existing Source/Spark test-internal payload/compute counters were not measured;
their success status is not a zero-operation attestation. The hosted job's accepted
software acquisition and unchanged Source/Spark dependency traffic were authorized;
they are distinct from bounded local metadata/aggregate response accounting.

No guardian-death, whole-job cancellation cleanup, source immutability or
whole-job cumulative-write-quota proof is claimed. Existing provider action
tags and disposable-host isolation remain the explicit trust premises.

## Next existing Gate 5 prerequisite

The next work is real-input read-only mount/private-ownership compatibility,
full-size resource admission, and a separately versioned real-import runtime
contract. The current real `run_import` entrypoint still rejects with
`host_guard_not_bound`; changing an approval flag cannot unlock it.

Local control-only preparation can define that successor. A dedicated host,
S3/model/tokenizer acquisition, real mount/import, GPU or training requires new
scope and approval. After real import, the already documented GPU-worker,
private-data and CUDA/smoke prerequisites remain. This result does not skip them.

